 * 400, so there was no page 2 at all, AND the search box's own placeholder
 * ("Search mods, plugins, and more…") promises to search the catalogue, not
 * whatever 400-or-fewer rows happened to already be loaded — a client-side
 * `.filter()` over a partial array would silently under-report or entirely
 * miss real matches outside that window.
 *
 * So this is now a Server Component: `mods` is just the current page,
 * already filtered/sorted/paginated by `lib/mods-catalog.ts`'s
 * `queryCatalogMods()`, and every control here is a plain link or a native
 * GET `<form>` that re-requests the page with new searchParams — the same
 * pattern this codebase already uses for /blog's search+pager
 * (app/blog/page.tsx) and the admin tables (lib/pagination.ts). No client
 * JS is required for the store to work at all; QuickAddButton (the one
 * genuinely interactive bit — installing onto a real server) stays its own
 * small Client Component underneath.
 */
